# jemdoc: nofooter, nodefaultcss, noeqs, addcss{../blog-note}, addjs{../blog-sidebar}
= My Raycast Workflow
[../../blog.html ← Blogs] \M /updated 2026-08-16/

Here I record my Raycast settings on macOS -- partly as a reference for myself, partly in the hope that they can help others too. Nothing here requires a paid subscription. I strongly recommend giving Raycast a try: it is genuinely great software and a real productivity boost.

== AI Configuration

Raycast AI accepts any OpenAI-compatible provider through custom providers, and the whole setup takes three steps.

~~~
{}{raw}
<h3 class="step-heading" id="step-1">Step 1: Enable custom providers</h3>
~~~

Turn on +Custom Providers+ under Raycast Settings -> AI -> Experiments.

~~~
{}{raw}
<h3 class="step-heading" id="step-2">Step 2: Edit the providers file</h3>
~~~
The file lives at +\~\/.config\/raycast\/ai\/providers.yaml+ (copy from +providers.template.yaml+ in the same folder). It declares a +providers+ list, each with +id+, +name+, +base_url+, +api_keys+, and +models+ (+id+, +name+, +provider+ mapping to a key, +context+, +abilities+):

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="copy-block">
<details>
<summary><span class="copy-block-marker">▸</span><span class="copy-block-title">Example <tt>providers.yaml</tt> (DeepSeek, replace YOUR_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY with a key from platform.deepseek.com/api_keys)</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="copy-providers" aria-label="Copy to clipboard"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6.75C0 5.784.784 5 1.75 5h1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-1.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v1.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 16h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 14.25Z"></path><path d="M5 1.75C5 .784 5.784 0 6.75 0h7.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 11h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 5 9.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Z"></path></svg></button></summary>
<pre id="copy-providers">providers:
  - id: deepseek
    name: DeepSeek
    base_url: https://api.deepseek.com
    api_keys:
      deepseek: YOUR_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY
    models:
      - id: deepseek-v4-flash
        name: DeepSeek V4 Flash Li
        provider: deepseek
        description: Fast, cost-efficient DeepSeek model, supports thinking mode
        context: 1000000
        abilities:
          temperature:
            supported: true
          vision:
            supported: false
          system_message:
            supported: true
          tools:
            supported: true
          reasoning_effort:
            supported: true</pre>
</details>
</div>
~~~

~~~
{}{raw}
<h3 class="step-heading" id="step-3">Step 3: Switch the model pickers to the new model</h3>
~~~

Restart Raycast, add the DeepSeek provider in the custom providers settings, then set +Quick AI+, +AI Chat+, and +AI Command+ to this model. Append your own suffix to a model +name+ (like +Li+ above) so same-name models from different providers stay distinguishable. Keys are plaintext on disk, so keep them local and out of any public page.

== Core Hotkeys

The only hotkey I set is +Command-Space+ to summon Raycast, replacing Spotlight (whose shortcut is disabled under System Settings -> Keyboard Shortcuts -> Spotlight).

Nothing else -- no hotkeys for AI Chat, AI Command, code snippets, or any other command.

== Extensions

A running list of extensions I recommend, kept updated as I keep trying new tools:

- [https://www.raycast.com/jlrochin/mole Mole]
- [https://www.raycast.com/pabroux/keepassxc KeePassXC]
- [https://www.raycast.com/keito4/skills Skills]
- [https://www.raycast.com/exa_ai/exa-search Exa]
- [https://www.raycast.com/gebeto/translate Google Translate]
- [https://www.raycast.com/nhojb/brew Brew]
- [https://www.raycast.com/browser-extension Browser]
- [https://www.raycast.com/mooxl/coffee Coffee]
- [https://www.raycast.com/koinzhang/copy-path Copy Path]

== Customizations

All my custom commands share one naming rule: the suffix +for lzengan+. It keeps my own commands easy to recognize and manage, and typing +lz+ in Raycast instantly narrows down to them, so they are fast to find and fast to trigger -- which matters, since these are usually the commands I use most often.

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="section-anchor" id="ai-commands" aria-hidden="true"></div>
~~~

=== AI Commands

*How to create:* press +Command-Space+ to summon Raycast, type +Create AI Command+, and hit Enter.

*What is an AI Command:* an AI Command embeds live data from your system into the prompt through placeholders, then sends the combined text to the model. While writing the prompt, type +{+ to insert a placeholder; when the command runs, the placeholder is replaced by real data. The useful ones are:

- +{selection}+ -- the text currently selected in the frontmost app
- +{clipboard}+ -- the last copied text
- +{browser-tab}+ -- the content of the focused browser tab, as Markdown (needs the Raycast Browser Extension)
- +{argument}+ -- prompts you to type a value in the search bar before the command runs

*Where they shine:* quick jobs such as summarizing a long web page or polishing a draft prompt so it sounds more professional. The tasks themselves are trivial -- the real win is avoiding the friction of opening a separate agent or chat window and copy-pasting content around for something easy but frequent.

*My crafted AI commands:*

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="command-item">
<p><span class="command-label"><span class="command-key">⌘</span>Webpage summary for lzengan</span> &ndash; summarizes the current browser page into key points with a single call.</p>
<div class="copy-block">
<details>
<summary><span class="copy-block-marker">▸</span><span class="copy-block-title">Prompt (in Chinese)</span><button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy="copy-webpage-summary" aria-label="Copy to clipboard"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 6.75C0 5.784.784 5 1.75 5h1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-1.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-1.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0v1.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 16h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 14.25Z"></path><path d="M5 1.75C5 .784 5.784 0 6.75 0h7.5C15.216 0 16 .784 16 1.75v7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.25 11h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 5 9.25Zm1.75-.25a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v7.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25Z"></path></svg></button></summary>
<pre id="copy-webpage-summary">请阅读当前网页，用最容易理解的方式告诉我：这东西到底在讲什么。

网页内容：
{browser-tab}

把我当成第一次接触这个主题、但具备正常理解能力的人。不要假设我了解相关术语、研究背景或行业黑话。

你的目标不是完整复述，而是让我在 30 秒内建立一个正确的基本认识，然后决定要不要继续深入。

按下面的格式回答：

# 一句话说清楚

用一句非常具体的人话说明：

“它想解决什么问题，用了什么核心办法，最后有什么用。”

不要写“本文提出了一种新方法”这种没有实际信息的句子。

# 到底是怎么回事？

用 2–4 个短段落，把事情讲清楚：

- 原来有什么问题
- 作者或项目做了什么
- 它为什么可能有效
- 最终得到什么结果

优先使用具体例子或简单类比。遇到专业术语时，立即用一句人话解释；如果术语对理解主线不重要，直接省略。

不要按照原文顺序逐段总结，也不要把摘要翻译一遍。请重新组织信息，先讲最容易理解、最重要的因果关系。

# 我只需要记住

列出最多 3 点真正值得记住的内容。

每一点都必须包含实质信息，不要重复前面的表述，不要罗列次要细节。

# 靠谱吗？

用 2–4 句话直接评价：

- 它最有说服力的证据是什么
- 最大的疑点、局限或没有解决的问题是什么
- 作者的结论有没有超过现有证据

如果是论文，简要说明它在哪些数据或实验上进行了验证，但不要罗列所有数据集、指标和数字，只保留会影响判断的关键信息。

如果是 GitHub 项目，简要判断它是否成熟、适合谁，以及使用它可能遇到的主要问题。

如果是博客、公众号、知乎或社交媒体内容，区分哪些是事实，哪些只是作者的观点、经验或营销表达。

# 要不要继续看？

只能给出以下三个结论之一：

- 值得深入看
- 只需要看其中一部分
- 知道这些就够了

然后用一句话说明理由。如果值得继续看，指出最值得看的具体部分。

写作要求：

- 默认使用简体中文
- 像一个特别会讲解的朋友，而不是论文审稿人
- 先让人听懂，再追求完整
- 多用短句，避免大段文字
- 不堆砌术语、缩写、数据集名称和实验指标
- 不使用“赋能、范式、维度、深度剖析”等空泛表达
- 不写传统学术摘要
- 不写面面俱到的检查清单
- 宁可省略次要内容，也不要淹没最核心的意思
- 整体尽量控制在一个屏幕左右
- 当前页面没有的信息不要猜；内容不完整时直接说明</pre>
</details>
</div>
</div>
~~~

